      "title": "13. Final recap",
      "content": [
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Remember the main workflow:"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Create: pvcreate → vgcreate → lvcreate"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Prepare and use: mkfs.xfs → mount"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Expand storage: vgextend if needed → lvextend → resize the file system"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Remove a physical volume: pvmove → vgreduce"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "The most important distinction in Chapter 7 is that the physical volume, volume group, logical volume, and file system are four different things. Knowing which layer you need to change helps you choose the correct command."
        },
